"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"51bd18d52cd0f3b68377ec2e219e0ffb346fe5d25774bc14f88144b749aedbae","event_uuid":"c09b72a6-addd-43f9-93b5-a168e7ed66e3","position":{"commit_sha":"8a63cf5cb9253470560f495c5e7b8e20e2baded2","position":"1788500312925906001-c09b72a6-addd-43f9-93b5-a168e7ed66e3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DUPLICATE of 477b-4130-424d-41eb (chiselled-thrifty-gnat), which was filed 14 seconds earlier by the agent that did the work, and which already carries file_impact and a discovered_from link to 9a17. My fault: I filed this without searching first, moments after the agent had filed its own. The two unique acceptance criteria from this ticket -- the defect-seeded mutation proof, and the requirement that the reproduction be deterministic rather than statistical -- have been copied onto 477b. Closing here; work 477b.","timestamp":1788500179624714001}],"completion_expectation":"disposition","created_at":1788499977370633001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c31f7b4a-be08-41a8-baf7-e4ad57e5824a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"477b-4130-424d-41eb"},{"link_uuid":"c53fa0d1-52ee-4790-b2a8-14da4cd0fbb4","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"477b-4130-424d-41eb"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\n`provision_toolchain` in `tests/e2e/_toolchain.py` (around `:151`) runs its fast-path `_satisfied()`\ncheck **before** taking the `flock`, and treats the bundle as ready on mere existence. A worker can\ntherefore observe a partially-written `node_modules`/`dist`, conclude provisioning is done, return\nearly, and run tests against a bundle another worker is still writing.\n\nFlagged as an advisory by the LLM reviewer on Gerrit change 2600 patchset 3, and judged a real defect\nrather than a style note by the implementing agent.\n\n## Why it was not fixed in 2600\n\nChange 2600 is the fix for bug `9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091`, which was failing ~46% of CI runs repo-wide and\nblocking every open change. Pushing a further patchset would have reset its `LLM-Review +1` and cost\nanother full review plus CI cycle on the change that was unblocking the repository. The deliberate\ncall was to land 2600 and track this separately.\n\n**This is not a regression introduced by 2600.** Before that change there was no lock at all and\nworkers raced freely; 2600 narrowed the window substantially. This ticket closes the remainder.\n\n## Fix shape\n\nDrop the unlocked fast path and perform the `_satisfied()` check **inside** the lock. An `flock` on a\nlocal file costs microseconds and is taken a handful of times per run, so the fast path buys\nnegligible time while creating the window.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAll deterministic and verifiable in a single run — no \"run it a few times and see\".\n\n1. A test demonstrates the race deterministically **before** the fix: one worker is made to observe\n   the partially-written state (e.g. hold the lock while a bundle is half-created, or stub the\n   filesystem state the fast path inspects) and is shown returning early. RED first — a race\n   asserted only by repetition is not a reproduction.\n2. After the fix, the same test shows the second worker blocking on the lock and observing only a\n   complete bundle.\n3. The existing provisioning behaviour is unchanged for the uncontended case: `tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py`\n   still passes in full, and a cold single-worker run still provisions exactly once.\n4. **Defect-seeded**: restoring the unlocked fast path makes AC1's test fail again. Demonstrated by\n   mutation, then reverted.\n5. No new mechanism is registered — this should be a movement of an existing check, not new\n   machinery. Verify with `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **and** `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`\n   (the latter is not covered by `make lint`).\n\n## Note\n\n`tests/e2e/_toolchain.py` and its lock were introduced by change 2600; read that change first for the\nsurrounding design, including why provisioning moved out of the fixture into\n`pytest_collection_modifyitems` and why a failed pre-provision must degrade to the in-fixture path\nrather than fail the step.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","477b-4130-424d-41eb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e7277535-c5c9-45fb-9867-70547b74be90","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bug","tests","e2e","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"c5ca-b32b-5e9e-4053","ticket_type":"bug","title":"e2e toolchain provisioning has an unlocked fast path: a worker can run against a bundle another worker is still writing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3837bcd8-793f-4a2d-9fec-9123247c4609","a2de0374-4377-46e2-a084-32abdafb752c","c31f7b4a-be08-41a8-baf7-e4ad57e5824a","c53fa0d1-52ee-4790-b2a8-14da4cd0fbb4","e7277535-c5c9-45fb-9867-70547b74be90","c09b72a6-addd-43f9-93b5-a168e7ed66e3"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788502850579662361,"uuid":"73cb40ad-3f51-4e0e-b684-c9a835cfc39f"}